'use strict';
// Expanded room descriptions (MULTIVERSE MUD setting). Keyed by room id; applied by areas.js. Edit and `update` to reload.
const D = {};
// ---------------- Ashfall (the sprawl) ----------------
Object.assign(D, {
  'town/square': "Rain-slick plascrete spreads out under a canopy of buzzing neon signs and old brass lanterns that nobody ever took down. A cracked stone fountain still runs at the center, its glowing water said to heal any traveler (type `drink fountain`), ringed by street vendors, off-duty guards and kids selling counterfeit charms. Skyscraper shadows from the corporate towers to the north swallow the sun by midafternoon. Chimneys, antennas and prayer flags share the same rooftops, and the air tastes of ozone, frying noodles and wet stone.",
  'town/gate': "A squat gatehouse of black composite stands where the sprawl meets the dead green belt beyond. Floodlights sweep the road, and a bored guard in scuffed armor checks credit chips more carefully than faces. Hand-painted warnings in six languages list what has been seen on the Forest Path lately. To the west a side door leads to the Dawn Clinic, and a gravel track to the east drops toward the old quarry.",
  'town/market': "Market Row is a canyon of awnings, rolling shutters and flickering holo-menus. Apothecaries, fixers and street docs hawk stims, power cells and herbal remedies from crates stacked three high. One stall still sells the good stuff under a hand-painted sign. Type `list` to see what is for sale, `buy` to purchase and `sell` to unload your spare salvage. The smell of cloves, solder and fry oil hangs thick, and somewhere a speaker is playing something with too much bass.",
  'town/inn': "The Silver Spur Saloon is a low, warm bar built into the shell of an old transit depot, all copper pipes, mismatched stools and a fire in a repurposed turbine housing. Mara runs the room with one hand and the peace with the other, and nobody fights under her roof. Cooks, couriers and runners drink in uneasy truce while a cracked jukebox hums in the corner. You mend faster here than anywhere else in the sprawl. A grimy door at the back opens onto a neon-lit clinic.",
  'town/smithy': "Brann's Smithy glows orange at the back, where a dented forge hammers out blades, plates and the odd weapon mount for a cyberarm. The walls are racks of salvaged armor and rusted tools, and soot has long since claimed the ceiling. A free rack by the door holds plain starter gear for newcomers who cannot afford better, and Brann sells proper blades from the counter. Type `list` to see his stock. Cooling steel ticks and sparks hiss on the damp floor.",
  'town/quarry': "A wide pit of broken grey stone beside the road, scarred by a century of cut and haul. Rusted tracks run to the lip of a shaft in the far wall, and the faces glitter with iron seams. Local scavengers work the edges with picks and hand drills, but the deeper tunnels belong to something else. Dust coats everything, drifting in the light of a distant floodlamp, and the clang of metal echoes off the pit walls.",
  'town/temple': "The Temple of the Dawn is an old stone chapel that now doubles as the best free clinic in the sprawl. Tall windows throw pale light across rows of cots, a humming med-scanner and an altar covered in candles, charms and donated stims. Sister Elara and her volunteers patch up anyone who walks in bleeding. Type `pray` to be fully healed and refreshed, free up to level 15 and for a small fee after. The air smells of antiseptic and incense.",
  'town/armory': "The Ironbound Armory is a narrow hall lined from floor to ceiling with ballistic vests, helmets, riot shields and boots on hooks. A sullen armorer sizes up every customer like a tailor and quotes prices in a flat voice. Type `list` to see what is for sale, and `sell` to offload gear you have outgrown. A single hanging lamp swings in the draft, and the whole room smells of oil, leather and cold metal.",
  'town/eastgate': "A wide arch of poured concrete opens onto the old interstate, the only road that leads out of Ashfall to the east. Merchants argue with border guards over tolls under flickering floodlights, and convoys of battered trucks queue in the mud. A rusted sign lists distances to places that no longer have names. The air smells of diesel and wet asphalt, and the road ahead disappears into dusk.",
  'town/clinic': "A neon-lit ripperdoc clinic behind the Silver Spur Saloon. Surgical chairs, humming coolers and shelves of glistening chrome fill the cramped room, and a doctor who asks no questions hums over a tray of instruments. Type `list` for cyberware, `install <name>` to buy and fit it, and `uninstall <name>` to remove it for a 50% refund. Chrome costs Aura, and less Aura means a smaller mana pool, so choose carefully.",
  'town/adventurers_guild': "The Guild is a converted warehouse with a cavernous main floor, a battered bar and a huge corkboard covered in jobs. Runners swap rumors over tabletops carved with old initials, and weapons hang in racks by the door. Fixer Torv sits behind a steel desk, watching everyone and trusting no one. Type `board` to read the open contracts, then talk to the person who posted them. The room smells of gun oil, coffee and rain.",
  'town/cobbler_lane': "A cramped lane where the shop fronts lean over each other like old friends. Cobblers, tinkers and tailors repair boots, bags and armor under flickering awnings, and the smell of leather glue hangs in the damp air. Cats and kids dart between stacked crates while a tired vendor argues with a customer about a sole. A single neon sign in the shape of a boot buzzes overhead.",
  'town/coopers_yard': "A walled yard stacked with barrels, kegs and water tanks in every state of repair. The cooper hammers staves into place with a rhythm like a heartbeat, and the smell of fresh oak and wet char hangs in the air. Salvaged pipes run along the walls, dripping into buckets. Hand-lettered signs advertise rainwater, filtered and unfiltered, with a warning about the second kind.",
  'town/bakers_row': "Warm light and the smell of real bread spill from the ovens that line this narrow street. Bakers shout prices over the noise, and a line of workers, couriers and street kids snakes out the door of the busiest shop. Steam curls from vents overhead, mixing with the neon glow of the signs. It is one of the few places in Ashfall where nobody is trying to sell you anything but breakfast.",
  'town/chapel_garden': "A small walled garden behind the temple, kept alive by volunteers with more love than money. Raised beds of herbs, bright flowers and tough little vegetables grow under a canopy of salvaged glass panels. A cracked statue of a forgotten saint watches over a bench. It is quiet here, the sprawl's noise reduced to a hum, and the smell of damp earth is a small mercy.",
  'town/watchtower': "A steel lattice tower bolted to the edge of the city wall, topped with floodlights, scanners and a rusted antenna farm. Guards climb the ladders in shifts, scanning the dark beyond the gate for anything that moves. From the platform you can see the glow of the sprawl behind you and the black line of the forest ahead. The wind up here carries sirens and wolf-song in equal measure.",
  'town/old_well': "A circular plaza around an ancient stone well, capped with a steel lid and a sign that warns against drinking from it. Old women sell charms and gossip from folding chairs, and children play a game with bottle caps in the dust. The well is older than the sprawl, older than the corporate towers, and some say older than the road. Rumor says it hums on certain nights.",
  'town/stables': "A long, low building that smells of hay, oil and animal sweat. Mutant mules, retrofitted mares and one very old cyber-horse stamp in their stalls, and the stablemaster oils a harness at a workbench. Tires, tools and saddles hang from every beam. The only sound is the shifting of hooves and the hum of a space heater nobody has switched off since winter.",
  'town/alchemists_tower': "A crooked brick tower leaning against a modern apartment block, every floor lit by a different colored lamp. The alchemist's workshop at the base is a mess of glass tubing, beakers, centrifuges and stacks of notebooks. Faint blue smoke curls from a copper still, and something in a jar on the shelf looks back at you. The whole building hums with a low, nervous energy.",
  'town/back_alley': "A narrow alley between two blank walls, lit by one flickering bulb and a patch of neon from a window above. Puddles reflect pink and blue in the dark. Bundled shapes sleep in doorways, and a drone with a broken rotor sits upside down in a dumpster. Everyone here has a reason to be somewhere else, and nobody asks yours. The sprawl feels very large and very close.",
});
// ---------------- Whisperwood (forest) ----------------
Object.assign(D, {
  'forest/path': "A rutted track under black pines, once the service road for a corporate green belt and now a pocked scar through the trees. Cracked asphalt shows through the needles, and rusted sensor posts lean at odd angles. Something skitters in the undergrowth and the wind carries the smell of damp earth and old machine oil. The glow of the sprawl fades behind you, and the forest closes in.",
  'forest/pond': "A still pond ringed with reeds, a short walk off the road. Trout flicker beneath the lily pads, and a rusted drone lies half-sunk at one edge, its camera eye green with algae. Dragonflies skim the surface, and the quiet is broken only by the plop of fish. It is a rare peaceful spot in the Reserve, popular with anglers and cautious scavengers.",
  'forest/clearing': "Pale light spills through a gap in the canopy onto a wide, trampled clearing where four trails meet. Old corporate signage lies face-down in the grass, and a cluster of goblin totems hangs from the trees to mark the territory. Tracks of boots, paws and claws cross the dirt in all directions. The forest hums with insects, and something watches from the shadows.",
  'forest/thicket': "Thorns snag at your sleeves in this dense tangle of brambles, where crude goblin totems hang from the branches by wire and string. The ground is littered with bones, scrap and the husks of old electronics, scavenged and half-forgotten. Smoke from a hidden fire drifts through the leaves, and the air is thick with the smell of burnt plastic.",
  'forest/stream': "A glassy stream runs over mossy stones, cold enough to ache. Wolf tracks pad down to the water's edge, and the banks are scarred by claw marks. On the far side a rusted pipe juts from the earth, trickling something that smells faintly of chemicals. The water gurgles on through the trees, and the way east leads toward the fog.",
  'forest/deep': "The trees crowd close and the air smells of wet stone and old moss. Little light reaches the forest floor, and the path is half-swallowed by ferns and roots. Feral eyes glint from the dark, and the howl of something large echoes in the distance. The path climbs toward a ruin that most locals refuse to name.",
  'forest/ruins': "A roofless chapel stands on a rise above the trees, its walls blackened and its windows long gone. Vines cling to the stonework, and a pile of rubble marks where the altar once stood. Behind it, a stair spirals down into the dark, and a cold draft rises from below. Old candle stubs and recent boot prints suggest the place is not quite abandoned.",
  'forest/mossy_hollow': "A low hollow thick with emerald moss, where sound dies the moment it leaves your mouth. Fallen logs are furred in green and the air feels damp and close. Mushrooms glow faintly along the roots, casting a ghostly blue light. Tiny feet scurry in the leaf litter, and the hollow smells of earth and slow rot.",
  'forest/fern_dell': "A shaded dell filled with waist-high ferns that rustle even when there is no wind. Shafts of light pierce the canopy and catch drifting spores like dust. Footpaths worn by animals crisscross the floor, and an old rusted fence line runs through the middle, wire long since swallowed by roots. It smells of cool green and rich earth.",
  'forest/hunters_blind': "A rough platform of bolted planks and scavenged metal sits in the crook of a huge oak, screened by branches and old camouflage netting. Someone left spent shells, a broken scope and a half-finished map of the animal trails below. From up here you can see for a hundred meters in any direction, and every noise in the forest comes to you clear.",
  'forest/fallen_giant': "A colossal pine lies across the trail, its trunk wider than a truck and its root ball tall as a house. Smaller trees have sprouted along its length, and the air is thick with the smell of sap and rot. Beneath the roots a dry hollow shows signs of use, with bones, feathers and scraps of scavenged cloth scattered inside.",
  'forest/twilight_glade': "A glade where the light always seems to be fading, lit by drifting motes and the pale glow of strange flowers. The air hums softly, as if the clearing were listening. Old standing stones ring the center, carved with symbols that predate the sprawl. Animals avoid the place, and so do most sensible runners.",
  'forest/spider_grove': "Thick webs stretch between the trees like sheets of grey gauze, heavy with dew and the husks of caught prey. Bundles of silk hang from the branches, some of them uncomfortably man-shaped. The air is still and sticky, and the faint rustle of many legs comes from above. Every step feels like trespass.",
  'forest/owl_roost': "A tall dead pine rises above the canopy, studded with hollows where owls and bats nest. Pellets and feathers carpet the ground, and the sound of soft wingbeats drifts down from the branches. A rusted radio mast stands nearby, its antenna wrapped in vines, still blinking a single faint red light. The air smells of dust and old nests.",
  'forest/hermits_clearing': "A small clearing tended with obvious care, ringed by raised herb beds and strings of drying leaves. A battered camper shell serves as a cabin, its roof covered in moss, and a stew pot simmers over a ring of stones. Old Fenwick lives here, and his wards keep the worst of the forest at bay. A small camp here offers safe rest and a chance to catch your breath.",
  'forest/hollow_oak': "An ancient oak, split and hollowed by lightning, stands alone in a ring of bare earth. The interior is large enough to shelter a dozen people, its walls smooth and polished by generations of hands. Carvings, initials and faded charms cover the wood. It smells of dry bark and woodsmoke, and a thin trail of ants marches across the floor.",
  'forest/thornwall': "A wall of black thorns, thick as a man's arm and sharp as razor wire, marks the edge of the Reserve's safe ground. Old corporate fencing is tangled in it, rusted and half-swallowed. Beyond lies country that even the goblins avoid. The thorns shift slightly when you are not looking, and the air tastes metallic and cold.",
});
// ---------------- Barrow Crypts ----------------
Object.assign(D, {
  'crypt/entry': "Cold air rises from the stair, carrying the smell of dust, old stone and something sweeter. Bones lie scattered at the foot of the steps, and the walls are scratched with desperate marks. Far below, a faint green glow flickers and fades. The sounds of the surface die behind you, and the dark seems to listen.",
  'crypt/hall': "Rows of sealed urns line the walls of this long vaulted hall, each carved with a name worn smooth by time. Several lids have been pushed aside from the inside. Cracked tile covers the floor, and a ribbon of old subway track runs through the center, reminding you that this place was once part of something larger. Doors lead east, west and south.",
  'crypt/bones': "Skulls are stacked to the ceiling in patient, horrible rows, thousands of them, their empty sockets turned toward the door. Someone has arranged them in patterns that hurt to look at. The air is dry and tastes of chalk, and a rattling noise comes from the dark at the far end of the room, where something is moving among the bones.",
  'crypt/cells': "Narrow stone cells line a corridor, each with a slab and a name worn away by time. Iron doors hang open, rust running down their hinges, and the floor is littered with scraps of cloth and splintered bone. A faint moaning comes from the end of the passage. The cold here is more than temperature.",
  'crypt/throne': "A throne of fused bone dominates the circular chamber, its arms carved into clutching hands and its back into a ribcage. Faded banners hang from the ceiling, and rusted weapons are heaped in the corners. The air is thick with old magic and the hum of failing machinery, as if the crypt had been wired into the throne. Its occupant is already rising.",
  'crypt/collapsed_vault': "A vaulted chamber half buried by a ceiling collapse, with heaps of rubble blocking half the room. Shattered urns and burst coffins spill their contents across the floor. Dust hangs in the air, and old cables trail out of the stone, still faintly warm. Something has been digging through the rubble from the other side.",
  'crypt/weeping_chamber': "Water drips constantly from the ceiling into shallow pools, producing a soft, endless sound like quiet sobbing. The walls are slick with moisture and the stones are carved with mourners with their faces in their hands. The air is cold and wet and carries a faint, sorrowful whisper that you cannot quite make out.",
  'crypt/bone_gallery': "A long gallery whose walls are inlaid with bones in intricate designs, from floral spirals to grim lines of marching skeletons. Candles in brass sconces flicker with a cold blue flame. Dust covers everything but a path of footprints leading deeper in. The skulls seem to turn as you pass.",
  'crypt/sealed_passage': "A narrow passage blocked at one end by a sealed iron door, its surface etched with warding runes and faded warnings. Scratches on the inside suggest that the seal was meant to keep something in. Cold air hisses through the gap at the bottom, carrying a smell of old blood. The runes pulse faintly when you come near.",
  'crypt/embalming_room': "A tiled room with stone tables, drains in the floor and shelves of dusty jars. Rusted instruments hang from hooks, and the walls are stained with a century of grim work. A single flickering fluorescent tube casts a sickly light. The smell of chemicals and old preservation still clings to everything.",
  'crypt/altar_of_ash': "A round chamber with a stone altar heaped with grey ash, still faintly warm. Burnt offerings, melted candles and broken charms surround it. Soot streaks the ceiling, and the walls bear scorch marks in the shape of hands. A faint chanting seems to drift from nowhere, in a language that has not been spoken in ages.",
  'crypt/flooded_crypt': "Black water fills the floor of this crypt to knee height, cold and utterly still. Sarcophagi emerge from the surface like sunken boats, their lids slightly ajar. Ripples spread from something unseen, and the air tastes of metal and mold. A rotting wooden walkway skirts the wall, groaning under each step.",
  'crypt/ghoul_warren': "A maze of burrows and hollows gnawed through the old tombs, floored with bones, rags and muck. The smell is overwhelming, a thick mix of rot and animal musk. Scratch marks cover the walls, and the sound of wet chewing echoes from a dark side passage. Ghouls have made this place their home.",
  'crypt/reliquary': "A hushed chamber of glass-fronted cases holding relics of the old faith: bones in silver, scraps of cloth, tarnished rings. Candles burn in clean brass holders, and the floor has been swept. Brother Aldous tends the room with quiet devotion, and a small camp of cots and blankets offers safe rest. For once, the dead are quiet.",
  'crypt/shadowed_nave': "A vast nave of broken pillars and shattered pews, lit only by a faint glow from a cracked stained-glass window high above. Shadows move without anything to cast them. The air is cold, and a low organ note vibrates in the stone. At the far end an altar stands bare, and the dark behind it feels deeper than it should.",
});
// ---------------- Redrock Trail (the old interstate) ----------------
Object.assign(D, {
  'road/mile1': "The old interstate runs east from Ashfall, a cracked ribbon of asphalt littered with burned-out wagons and wrecked trucks in the ditch. Wind whips grit across the lanes, and crows pick at scraps on the shoulder. Road gangers lurk behind the wrecks, watching travelers with predatory patience. The glow of the sprawl falls away behind you.",
  'road/mile2': "Dry grass, crows and long shadows line the highway here. Rocks on the ridge above provide perfect cover for ambushers, and fresh tire tracks cut across the dirt. Torn banners flap from a leaning signpost. Somewhere out of sight, an engine idles, and the smell of burning fuel drifts down the road.",
  'road/fork': "A huge signpost, bent and rusted, stands at the crossroads, pointing north to the Frostpeak Pass and east to the Sunscorch Dunes. A gang warlord holds this junction with a ring of burned-out trucks and spiked barricades. Graffiti covers every flat surface, and the wind carries engine noise from both directions. This is the road's true crossing.",
  'road/burnt_wagon': "A charred wagon lies on its side, its wheels melted and its cargo scattered across the road. Footprints and shell casings mark where the attackers struck, and the smell of fuel and scorched metal lingers. A torn flag still clings to one corner, and something glints among the ashes. Whoever died here died fast.",
  'road/dry_wash': "A dry riverbed cuts under the road through a concrete culvert, littered with sun-bleached bones and old tires. Echoes carry strangely in the tunnel, and every step sounds like pursuit. Graffiti marks the walls in the signs of three different gangs. It is a perfect hiding place for anyone who does not want to be found.",
  'road/watch_hill': "A low hill beside the road, crowned by a rusted observation tower and a scatter of sandbags. From the top you can see the highway running for miles in both directions, and anything that moves leaves a plume of dust. Spent casings litter the platform. Someone is always watching, and everyone knows it.",
  'road/abandoned_inn': "A roadside inn with half its roof fallen and its sign hanging by one chain, yet someone has swept the floor and lit a stove. Greta keeps this place alive for stray travelers, with cots, a pot of stew and a shotgun behind the bar. A small camp here offers safe rest, and she hears every rumor on the road.",
  'road/bandit_camp': "A ring of dented trucks and scrap barricades surrounds a smoking fire pit, where gangers drink, argue and sharpen blades. Stolen goods are piled under tarps, and crude trophies hang from poles. Loud music blares from a battered speaker, hiding the sound of any approach. The place smells of smoke, fuel and old grudges.",
  'road/old_milestone': "A weathered concrete marker stands beside the road, its numbers rubbed away and replaced with crude graffiti. Someone has left a fresh bouquet of wilted flowers at its base. The wind sighs through the dry grass, and a lone crow watches from the top. It is a quiet spot, and an easy one to be ambushed in.",
  'road/shepherds_rest': "A small stone shelter with a patched tin roof stands beside a dry trough, built long ago for travelers and herders. Old blankets lie folded on a rough bench, and someone has scratched a map of the road on the wall. The place is poor, but the roof holds, and the wind sounds far away.",
  'road/ambush_gully': "The road dips into a narrow gully with steep banks on both sides, studded with rocks and brush. Everything about the spot seems designed for an ambush, and the scattered bones and rusted gear suggest it has been used for that very purpose. Footprints are fresh, and the quiet is too deliberate.",
  'road/toll_bridge': "A long steel bridge spans a dry ravine, with a toll booth at either end and a heavy chain across the road. The booths are riddled with bullet holes, and a rope still dangles from the rail. Under the bridge, the dry creek bed is littered with the wrecks of vehicles that did not pay. The wind moans in the girders.",
  'road/hanging_tree': "A gnarled, leafless tree stands alone beside the road, its lowest branch worn smooth by rope. Strips of faded cloth flutter from the twigs, and crows sit in a silent row along the limbs. Nobody lingers here. The air feels colder than it should, and the shadows lie in the wrong direction.",
});
// ---------------- Sunken Marsh (slag marsh) ----------------
Object.assign(D, {
  'marsh/edge': "The forest gives way to black water and drifting mist, where an old corporate runoff channel spills into a sprawling marsh. The ground turns soft and slick underfoot, and the air tastes of rust and rot. Dead trees stand like skeletal sentries in the shallows, and the croak of something large echoes across the fog.",
  'marsh/reeds': "Tall reeds hide things that ripple the water, and every sway might be the wind or something watching. The boardwalk here has half rotted away, leaving slippery gaps over dark water. Insects whine in clouds, and fish flash in the shallows. A rusty drum floats nearby, trailing a faint rainbow sheen across the surface.",
  'marsh/mire': "Each step sinks to the knee in thick, stinking mud, and bubbles of foul gas rise around you with soft pops. The air is thick, warm and rotten, and the pools shimmer with chemical colors. Crocodiles drift just under the surface, patient and silent. The mire has swallowed more than one careless runner.",
  'marsh/hut': "A rickety hut on stilts, hung with bones, drying herbs and strands of colored wire. A crooked ladder leads up to a door of scavenged metal, and smoke curls from a pipe chimney. Something bubbles in a cauldron on the porch, and the smell is both sweet and awful. The marsh hag lives here, and she does not like visitors.",
  'marsh/den': "A sinkhole of churned mud and broken stone, ringed by rotten timber and half-sunk wreckage. The ground is slick with slime, and the air is thick with the smell of something old and very large. Bones of unlucky travelers lie scattered in the muck. In the center, coils shift in the dark, and many heads turn toward you.",
  'marsh/sunken_boat': "A rusted fishing boat lies half sunk at the edge of a quiet inlet, its deck patched with scrap and its hull painted with faded names. Old Barnaby lives aboard, with nets, tools and a cookstove under a tarp. A small camp on the bank offers safe rest, and the sound of lapping water is oddly soothing.",
  'marsh/frog_pond': "A small pond choked with lily pads and shining with oily rainbows. Frogs of every size sing in the reeds, some with too many legs or too few. Dragonflies hover above the surface, their wings glinting like tiny blades. It would be peaceful if the water were not faintly glowing at night.",
  'marsh/rotting_pier': "A long wooden pier stretches into the marsh, its planks soft with rot and slick with slime. Old crates and rusted winches litter the end, and a skeleton in a ragged coat leans against a post. The boards groan with each step, and the dark water below stirs with something patient.",
  'marsh/fungus_grotto': "A hollow in the marsh bank filled with giant mushrooms that glow in blue, green and violet. Spores drift like snow, and the air is thick and warm. Strange tracks cross the soft floor, and the glow throws long shadows that seem to move on their own. Everything here smells of damp earth and sweet decay.",
  'marsh/peat_bog': "A wide, spongy bog where every step leaves a dark, water-filled print. Pale bones and the occasional bronze relic poke from the surface, preserved by the acid water. The ground quivers, and a thin mist rises from the pools. It is easy to lose your footing, and harder to get it back.",
  'marsh/heron_rookery': "Tall dead trees rise from the shallows, heavy with the nests of herons and egrets. The air is loud with squawks and the flap of wings, and the water below is white with droppings. The birds are watchful and fierce, and the only things in the marsh that do not seem afraid of you.",
  'marsh/witch_lights': "Pale lights drift across the water, hovering and bobbing like lanterns carried by invisible hands. They lead the unwary toward deeper water, and the marsh is littered with the things that followed them. The air hums, the mist tastes of copper, and for a moment you almost hear voices calling your name.",
  'marsh/drowned_chapel': "A stone chapel stands half sunk in the marsh, its roof gone and its pews rotted into green slime. Water laps at the altar, and a bell hangs silent in the fallen tower. Pale shapes drift in the flooded nave, and the walls are covered in faded murals of saints with their faces worn away.",
  'marsh/muddy_causeway': "A raised track of packed earth and old concrete runs through the marsh, rutted by wheels and cracked by roots. The sides drop away into stinking water, and fog hangs thick in the low spots. Footprints, claw marks and tire tracks overlap in the mud. It is the only safe way through, and everything knows it.",
  'marsh/leech_pool': "A dark, still pool fringed with reeds, its surface strangely smooth. The water is thick with fat leeches the length of a forearm, writhing in the shallows. The bank is bloodstained, and animal bones lie bleached nearby. Tiny ripples spread from the center, and the smell is rank.",
});
// ---------------- Silverado Mines ----------------
Object.assign(D, {
  'mines/entry': "Rusted rails lead into a timbered tunnel mouth, its entrance framed by warning signs in faded paint. Cold air flows out, carrying the smell of iron, damp and old machine oil. A broken ore cart lies on its side near the gate, and the dark beyond seems to swallow the light of your lamp. Something scuttles in the shadows.",
  'mines/tunnel': "A collapsed section of tunnel, where the timber supports have fallen and the ceiling sags dangerously. Webs hang thick across the beams, and the floor is littered with chunks of rock and old tools. Water drips from the ceiling, and the air is close and heavy. Every sound is swallowed by the stone.",
  'mines/shaft': "A huge vertical shaft drops into blackness, with a rusted lift cage hanging over the edge by a single cable. Old signs warn of death for anyone who rides it, and the cable creaks in the draft. Wind howls up from below, cold and smelling of deep earth. A narrow ledge runs along the wall.",
  'mines/forge': "A dwarven forge sits cold in the center of a wide chamber, its anvil still ringing when struck and its chimney choked with soot. Tools hang on the walls in careful order, and the floor is littered with half-finished work. Great stone golems stand in alcoves, motionless and patient. A working forge is here for those who know how to use it.",
  'mines/vault': "Silver veins glitter in the walls of this great vault, lit by the faint glow of crystals in the ceiling. Chests of ore, coin and old gear are heaped around a throne carved from the rock itself. A crowned figure guards the place, huge and patient, and the air hums with the weight of old greed.",
  'mines/ore_cart_track': "Rusted rails run along the tunnel floor, bent and broken in places, and a line of abandoned ore carts sits rotting in the dark. The walls are scarred with pick marks, and old lamps hang from hooks, long dead. A faint breeze carries the echo of metal on stone.",
  'mines/flooded_drift': "A low drift tunnel, flooded to the knee with cold, silent water that reflects your light like black glass. Old pumps and pipes rust along the wall, and the ceiling drips steadily. Pale cave fish dart around your ankles, and the water level seems to be slowly rising.",
  'mines/timber_cavern': "A wide cavern propped up by a forest of rough timber beams, many of them split or rotten. Sawdust and dust coat everything, and the air smells of old pine and damp earth. Every creak sounds like the beginning of a collapse, and the shadows between the supports feel crowded.",
  'mines/crystal_seam': "A rich seam of glittering crystal runs through the wall, casting soft colored light across the cavern. The crystals hum faintly, resonating with the air, and the surface is cool to the touch. Miners long ago scratched warning marks around the vein. The glow makes your shadow stretch strangely across the stone.",
  'mines/foremans_office': "A cramped office carved into the rock, with a battered desk, a sagging cot and a wall of faded maps. Foreman Durn keeps the place tidy, with a stove, a kettle and a shelf of dusty ledgers. A small camp here offers safe rest, and the sounds of the mine feel far away.",
  'mines/dripping_gallery': "A long gallery where the ceiling drips constantly, forming small pools in the uneven floor. Stalactites hang like teeth overhead, and the air is damp and cold. Every drop echoes, making it impossible to tell whether something is following you. The walls shine with moisture and the faint glint of minerals.",
  'mines/narrow_crawl': "A narrow crawlway so low you must stoop and twist to pass, its walls rubbed smooth by generations of miners. Your lamp barely lights a meter ahead, and the sound of your breathing is loud in the dark. Claustrophobia presses in, and something scratches faintly in the rock beyond.",
  'mines/smelter_hall': "A cavernous hall dominated by a huge, dead smelter, its furnace doors hanging open and its chimney vanishing into the dark. Old slag heaps spill across the floor, still faintly warm. Heavy chains dangle from gantries, swaying slightly in the draft. The air smells of cold ash and old metal.",
  'mines/collapsed_stope': "A huge chamber half filled by a cave-in, with a slope of broken rock rising to the ceiling. Dust settles slowly in the lamplight, and the stone groans as it shifts. Bones and broken tools poke from the rubble. The collapse was not an accident, and it is not entirely finished.",
  'mines/echoing_chamber': "A vast round chamber where every sound returns as a hundred whispers. Your footsteps clatter back from the walls in layered echoes, and your own voice answers from the dark. Old mining machinery rusts in the corners, and the floor is polished smooth by the passage of many feet.",
});
// ---------------- Sunscorch Dunes ----------------
Object.assign(D, {
  'dunes/oasis': "A walled oasis of tents, fountains and neon-lit stalls, where traders from across the wastes sell gear for travelers heading deeper. Palm trees shade a clear pool, and a bazaar of striped awnings crowds the paths. The air is full of spice, solder and haggling in a dozen languages. Type `list` to see what the traders are selling.",
  'dunes/sands': "Heat shimmers over endless dunes of rust-colored sand, scattered with the bones of vehicles and men. The sun hammers down without mercy, and the wind sculpts the ground into endless ripples. Scorpions as large as dogs scuttle between the dunes, their armor glinting like chrome. Every direction looks identical.",
  'dunes/obelisk': "A black obelisk rises from the sand, glossy and warm to the touch, carved with spiraling text in a forgotten tongue. A faint hum emanates from the stone, and the air around it shimmers. Wraiths drift near the base, half seen and wholly hostile. The sand here is dark and strangely cold.",
  'dunes/ruins': "Half-buried columns and fallen walls frame a wide staircase leading down into darkness. The sand has swallowed most of the ancient city, leaving only fragments of paving and the heads of great statues. The stair is smooth, steep and ominous, and the air from below is dry and ancient. Something moves in the shade.",
  'dunes/tomb': "A vast burial chamber glittering with gold and lapis, its walls covered in vivid murals of kings and gods. Rows of canopic jars line the walls, and a huge sarcophagus dominates the center. The lid is already moving, and the chamber fills with a dry, whispering voice. The pharaoh has woken.",
  'dunes/cracked_dune': "A dune split by an ancient crack, its flanks crusted with dried salt and broken glass. Footprints of long-dead travelers are fossilized in the clay. The wind howls through the fissure, and the air tastes of dust and iron. It is a landscape built by heat and time.",
  'dunes/dry_well': "A stone well rises from the sand, its rope long rotted and its bucket buried. The shaft drops into dry, echoing darkness, and old bones lie scattered at the lip. Someone scratched a warning on the rim in several languages. The wind stirs sand inside the well, producing a low, mournful sound.",
  'dunes/caravan_graveyard': "The skeletons of ancient trucks, wagons and armored crawlers lie half buried in the dunes, their metal bleached and pitted. Bones, bottles and torn canvas flutter in the wind. A lone satellite dish stands upright, pointed at nothing. The place is silent, and anything of value was stripped long ago.",
  'dunes/scorched_mesa': "A flat-topped mesa of red stone, baked by the sun and streaked with glassy black seams. The surface is almost too hot to touch, and shimmering waves rise from the rock. Lizards dart between the cracks, and a lone vulture circles high above. The view from the top reaches to the horizon.",
  'dunes/sand_pit': "A deep funnel of loose sand, its sides trickling constantly toward a dark hole at the bottom. Bones, rusted gear and scraps of cloth are half buried around the rim. Something lies waiting beneath the surface, and the sand shifts when you step too close. It would be very hard to climb out.",
  'dunes/nomad_camp': "A ring of tents of patched canvas and salvaged tarp, with a cookfire at the center and camels, buggies and goats tethered nearby. Sheikh Rashid sits beneath an awning, sipping tea and listening to the news of the road. A small camp here offers safe rest, and the hospitality is genuine if watchful.",
  'dunes/whispering_dune': "A tall dune whose slopes hum and whisper as the wind passes over them, a sound like distant voices speaking in an unknown tongue. The sand shifts constantly, forming and unforming faint shapes. Travelers say the voices speak secrets, and some say they speak your name. It is easy to lose track of time here.",
  'dunes/broken_statue': "A colossal stone statue lies shattered in the sand, its head half buried and its hand raised in a gesture of stern command. Inscriptions in several scripts cover the base, long since worn into illegibility. A nest of vultures occupies the shoulder, and the shadow of the head is the only shade for miles.",
  'dunes/salt_flat': "A dazzling white plain of cracked salt stretches to the horizon, blinding in the sun. The ground crunches underfoot, and the heat rises in waves that distort everything. Skeletons of animals lie scattered where they fell, preserved by the salt. There is no cover and no water, and every step feels exposed.",
  'dunes/mirage_gate': "Two weathered stone pillars stand in the sand like the remnants of a gate, with the air between them rippling like water. Visions of green lawns and cool pools appear and vanish in the shimmer. Many have walked through chasing the vision. The sand around the pillars is littered with the things they left behind.",
});
// ---------------- Frostpeak ----------------
Object.assign(D, {
  'frost/lodge': "A stone and steel lodge hunkered against the mountain, its windows glowing warm against the snow. A fire roars in the hearth, and mountaineers in heated parkas pack gear and swap warnings over steaming mugs. Maps, ice axes and frost-bitten trophies cover the walls. Outfitters here sell strong equipment to anyone with the nerve for the pass. Type `list` to see what is for sale.",
  'frost/pass': "Wind howls through a narrow, icy gap in the mountains, carrying needles of snow that sting exposed skin. The path is slick with ice, and old safety cables hang rusted and frozen from the rock. Wolf tracks are everywhere, and the howls echo off the cliffs. Visibility drops to a few meters in the worst gusts.",
  'frost/ledge': "A narrow ledge hugs the mountain, with a sheer drop on one side and an ice cave on the other. Frozen waterfalls hang like curtains, and the snow glitters in the thin light. A rusted ski lift tower stands crooked above, its cable snapped. Every step is a gamble, and the wind pulls at your clothing.",
  'frost/cave': "Blue crystals hum with cold light, studding the walls and ceiling of a huge ice cavern. The air is dry and bitingly cold, and your breath freezes in front of you. The crystals ring faintly in the draft, like a chorus of glass bells. Ore veins run through the rock behind the ice.",
  'frost/hall': "Icicles hang like spears over a vast hall carved from a glacier, with a throne of ancient ice at the far end. Frozen warriors stand in the walls, caught in mid-charge, and the floor is a polished mirror of blue. The air crackles with cold magic, and a thunderous breathing echoes from the dark ahead.",
  'frost/snowdrift_hollow': "A deep hollow filled with soft, powdery snow, sheltered from the worst of the wind. Footprints and animal tracks cross the surface, and a small pocket of warmth lingers near a rocky outcrop. It is easy to sink to the waist, and the silence presses against your ears. Something white shifts at the edge of sight.",
  'frost/frozen_waterfall': "A huge waterfall frozen in mid-fall, its ice layered in blues and whites and glittering in the sun. Icicles as thick as trees hang from the cliff, and the rock behind is slick with frost. The air hums with the cold, and cracks in the surface hint at the rushing water beneath.",
  'frost/avalanche_slope': "A wide slope of loose snow, marked by the scars of past avalanches and strewn with broken rock. Even a shout might bring the mountain down. Bones and bits of gear emerge from the surface, and the snow groans as it settles. Every step feels like it could be the last.",
  'frost/ice_bridge': "A natural bridge of ice spans a deep crevasse, blue-white and smooth as glass. Wind whistles through the chasm below, and the bridge creaks and pings underfoot. The far side seems very far away, and the drop is lost in darkness. Footprints in the frost show that others have crossed, and a few did not.",
  'frost/hermits_igloo': "A cozy igloo built into a snowbank, its entrance sealed with a thick fur flap and its roof topped by a thin chimney. Inside, Hermit Ulf tends a small stove, surrounded by furs, books and carved bone tools. A small camp here offers safe rest, and the warmth after the cold is almost painful.",
  'frost/glacier_crack': "A deep crack runs through the glacier, its walls shining blue and its depths black. The ice groans and shifts, sending tremors through the surface. Frozen things glimmer far below, caught in the ice, and the cold breath of the crevasse tugs at your feet. Do not look down for long.",
  'frost/windscoured_peak': "A bare peak scoured clean by the wind, with rock as smooth as glass and snow only in the deepest cracks. The world falls away on every side, and the sky seems close enough to touch. Frozen prayer flags crack in the gale, and the cold is so intense it burns. The view is magnificent and deadly.",
  'frost/frozen_camp': "The abandoned camp of an expedition, its tents torn and stiff with ice and its supplies frozen solid. Crates, cooking gear and rusted equipment are scattered about, and a journal lies open on a table, its last entries scrawled in panic. Something has been here since, and the footprints are far too large.",
  'frost/crystal_chasm': "A narrow chasm lined with giant crystals that glow in shifting blues and greens, casting rippling light across the ice. The air sings with a thin, high note, and the crystals shiver in response to your footsteps. Reflections multiply endlessly, making it hard to tell where the walls are.",
  'frost/blizzard_gap': "A narrow gap between two peaks where the wind funnels into a perpetual blizzard, so thick you can barely see your own hand. Snow stings your eyes, and the roar of the storm drowns every other sound. Shapes move at the edge of vision, and the cold seeps in through every layer.",
});
// ---------------- Ember Wastes (meltdown zone) ----------------
Object.assign(D, {
  'ember/gate': "Black rock and hot wind greet you at the edge of the Wastes, where an old reactor complex bled its fire into the land. The ground glows red in cracks and seams, and the air tastes of sulfur and burnt metal. Fire imps flit between the stones, cackling. Warning signs in a dozen languages lie bent and melted at the roadside.",
  'ember/ash': "Ankle-deep grey ash covers the plain, shifting with every step and kicking up clouds that sting the eyes. Burning things hunt in the haze, their eyes glowing red, and their howls echo across the dark. The sky is a smear of orange and black, and the ground is warm beneath your boots.",
  'ember/lava': "A river of molten rock crawls through a channel in the black stone, glowing orange and slow as syrup. Heat shimmers over the surface, and the air is too hot to breathe deeply. Elementals walk in the flow, shedding sparks, and the banks are scarred by their passage. The smell of hot metal is overpowering.",
  'ember/temple': "A temple of black iron stands in the Wastes, its walls blistered by heat and its doors twisted open. Inside, the forge at the center still burns with an unnatural flame, and the anvil is scarred with strange symbols. Figures in molten armor stand motionless in alcoves. A working forge is here for those who know how to use it.",
  'ember/caldera': "The mouth of a volcano yawns open under a boiling sky, a vast bowl of seething magma and drifting ash. Heat hammers at you, and the ground trembles with every roar from below. In the center, a figure of fire and stone rises from the lava, huge, burning and awake.",
  'ember/sulfur_vent': "A crack in the earth belches yellow gas, coating the surrounding rock in bright crystalline deposits. The smell is eye-watering, a stench of rotten eggs and hot metal. The ground is brittle and warm, and every few moments the vent hisses and spits. The air shimmers with heat and poison.",
  'ember/obsidian_field': "A wide field of black volcanic glass, polished by the wind and jagged as broken bottles. Reflections of the angry sky dance across the surface, and every step crunches loudly. Shards glitter like knives, and the heat rising from below makes the air waver. It is a beautiful and treacherous place.",
  'ember/lava_tube': "A tunnel formed by ancient lava flow, its walls smooth and glassy and its floor still warm. Glowing veins of orange run through the rock, casting a faint light, and heat shimmers in the air. The tube echoes with a low roar that grows louder as you advance. Something moves in the glow ahead.",
  'ember/scorched_camp': "A small camp of heat-proof tents and shielded gear, set in a sheltered nook of black rock. Pyromancer Sael tends a bubbling kettle and a bank of sensors, scribbling notes in a singed notebook. A small camp here offers safe rest, protected by wards that hum faintly in the heat.",
  'ember/basalt_steps': "A natural staircase of hexagonal basalt columns, climbing a steep slope of black rock. The steps are warm and slightly uneven, and a faint hiss rises from the cracks between them. The view from the top shows rivers of fire cutting through the plain, and the heat of the stone seeps through your boots.",
  'ember/smoking_crater': "A wide crater whose floor is cracked and glowing, with thick smoke rising from a dozen vents. The ground is soft and hot, and the air is thick and acrid. Cinders spit from the rim, and the sound of distant rumbling never stops. It is a dangerous place to linger, and few do.",
  'ember/ash_dune': "A great dune of fine grey ash, drifting under the wind like a slow ocean. It piles against old ruins and half buries the wrecks of burnt vehicles. The surface is soft and treacherous, hiding hollows and vents beneath, and the air is thick with fine powder that clogs the throat.",
  'ember/geyser_basin': "A basin of boiling pools and spouting geysers, rimmed with mineral crust in garish yellows and reds. Steam hangs in the air, and the ground shakes with each eruption. The water is scalding and strange, and the smell is thick and mineral. Timing your steps is the difference between safety and a nasty burn.",
  'ember/molten_pool': "A wide pool of glowing magma, bubbling gently and throwing off waves of heat. Black crust forms and cracks across the surface, and rivulets of fire trickle toward the edge. The air is almost too hot to stand. Things stir under the glow, drawn by the fire.",
  'ember/charred_grove': "A grove of blackened, skeletal trees, their trunks turned to charcoal and their branches reaching like claws. The ground is thick with ash, and a few embers still smolder in the roots. Ashen birds perch silent in the branches, and the air is hot, dry and heavy with the smell of old fire.",
});
// ---------------- Shattered Citadel (fallen corporate keep) ----------------
Object.assign(D, {
  'cit/gate': "A broken fortress of black stone and twisted steel looms over the road, its gatehouse cracked and its banners torn. The portcullis hangs bent, and the dead guard it with silent patience. Old corporate insignias are burned into the stone, long since defaced. The wind through the arch sounds like a faint, mournful chorus.",
  'cit/hall': "Torn banners hang from the high rafters over a vast hall of broken pillars and rows of empty armor. The floor is a mosaic of cracked tile showing a forgotten coat of arms. Sunlight slants through shattered windows, picking out dust and drifting ash. Doors lead in every direction, and the place feels watched.",
  'cit/library': "A ruined library of burned shelves and scattered books, its great windows shattered and its floor deep in ash. A wraith drifts through the stacks turning pages that are no longer there. Fragments of manuscripts and old data discs lie among the debris. Faint whispers rise from the dark corners, reading aloud forgotten words.",
  'cit/barracks': "Rows of cots in neat lines stretch along the walls, each with a folded blanket and a rusted weapon rack. Armor stands guard at attention between them, and faint footsteps sound from the empty rooms. Lockers hang open, their contents long since scattered. The air is cold and still, as if waiting for a bugle call.",
  'cit/throne': "A cold throne of black iron stands on a dais at the end of the great chamber, flanked by broken statues and faded banners. A spiral stair behind it descends into the dark, breathing a chill from below. The Dread Marshal waits here, armored in rust and iron, patient as the grave.",
  'cit/armory_ruins': "A wrecked armory, its racks overturned and its doors hanging from their hinges. Broken weapons and cracked armor litter the floor, and the smell of old oil and rust is strong. Scorch marks and bullet scars cover the walls, evidence of a last stand. Something metallic scrapes in the dark.",
  'cit/collapsed_rampart': "A section of the great wall has collapsed, leaving a ramp of rubble and twisted rebar. The wind whips across the gap, carrying the sounds of the plains far below. Arrow slits and cannon mounts stare at nothing, and gargoyles crouch on the broken edge, waiting for something to fall.",
  'cit/chapel_of_bells': "A small chapel whose bell tower has fallen in, leaving great bronze bells scattered across the floor. Pews are splintered, and the altar is cracked. When the wind blows, the broken bells ring faintly, a hollow and unsettling music. Faded murals show soldiers kneeling in prayer.",
  'cit/dungeon_stair': "A narrow stair descends into the dungeon under the keep, its steps worn by countless feet and slick with damp. Iron rings in the walls hold the stubs of torches, and scratches mark the stone. The air grows colder and the sound of dripping water echoes from below. It smells of rust and despair.",
  'cit/banquet_hall': "A long banquet hall, its table still laid with rotted food and tarnished silver. Candelabras hang from the ceiling, draped with cobwebs, and the chairs are pushed back as if the guests had risen all at once. The dust is undisturbed except for a trail of footprints leading to the head of the table.",
  'cit/war_room': "A circular room dominated by a great map table, its surface carved with the lines of old campaigns. Rusted markers and scattered orders lie across it, and the walls are hung with maps and tactical diagrams. Screens flicker with static, and a faint voice repeats orders to an army long dead.",
  'cit/cursed_gallery': "A long gallery lined with portraits of past lords, their faces scratched out or burned. The frames are cracked, and the eyes of those that remain seem to follow you. Cold air drifts through the room, and a whisper like muffled laughter runs along the walls. Something hangs behind the paint.",
  'cit/watchtower_top': "The top of the highest tower, open to the wind and the night sky. A rusted signal lamp stands on a stone pedestal, and the parapet is scarred with old battle damage. The land spreads out below, dark and ruined, with the glow of fire on the horizon. The wind howls like a living thing.",
  'cit/guard_post': "A cramped guardroom with a stove, a rack of weapons and a battered table covered in maps and notes. Sergeant Voss, the last living soldier of the garrison, keeps watch through a narrow window. A small camp here offers safe rest, and the wards on the door keep the dead at bay.",
  'cit/crypt_gate': "A heavy iron gate stands at the end of a short passage, sealed with chains and etched with warding runes. Beyond it, a stair leads down to the royal crypts. The air is bitterly cold, and the chains rattle faintly in the draft. Whatever lies below, it has not been disturbed in a very long time.",
});
// ---------------- The Abyss (the dark Net and the void beneath) ----------------
Object.assign(D, {
  'abyss/stair': "A black stair winds down into a place that was never meant to be seen. The steps are cold, smooth and faintly humming, and the walls give off a strange phosphorescence. Gravity feels uncertain, and the dark seems to breathe. Pale shapes drift on the edge of sight, and the air tastes of static and ash.",
  'abyss/rift': "Space tears and mends in a shifting wound across the chamber, spilling pale light and streaming code. Through it you glimpse landscapes that are neither fantasy nor machine, vast and wrong. Something huge moves behind the rift, and the air shudders with each of its motions. Time seems to stutter.",
  'abyss/core': "There is no floor here, only a will that wants everything to end. The Heart of the Void is a vast cavern of drifting darkness and slow, spinning lights, humming with a low note that rattles your bones. In the center, a figure of nothing waits, and every shadow bends toward it.",
  'abyss/whispering_void': "Voices drift through the dark, murmuring in half-formed sentences, some in tongues you almost recognize. The air is thick and cold, and the walls dissolve into drifting fog. Pale lights flicker and fade, and your own footsteps sound distant. The whispers seem to know you.",
  'abyss/fractured_stair': "A staircase broken into floating fragments, suspended in the dark with gaps between each step. Wind that is not wind pushes at you, and the stone hums with a thin, high note. Below, there is no bottom, only the shifting glow. Every step is a leap of faith.",
  'abyss/maw_of_stars': "A huge opening in the floor of reality, rimmed with teeth of crystal and edged with swirling light. Tiny stars spin in the abyss below, drawn toward the center in a slow spiral. The pull is gentle and constant. A single wrong step would send you drifting forever.",
  'abyss/weeping_chasm': "A chasm of black glass, its walls streaming with silver tears that fall upward into the dark. A low sobbing echoes along the cliff, soft and endless. The air tastes of salt and static, and shadows crouch on the ledges, listening. The place is full of unfinished sorrow.",
  'abyss/echo_chamber': "A perfectly round chamber where every sound repeats forever, bouncing from the walls in distorted loops. Your own footsteps return as a crowd, and your breath as a gale. The floor is polished obsidian, reflecting faces that are not yours. It is hard to think clearly in here.",
  'abyss/shadow_bridge': "A bridge of solid shadow stretches across an infinite gap, thin as a blade and cold as a grave. It sways faintly, and the void below breathes upward with a smell of old rain and hot wire. The far end is lost in fog. Something shifts beneath the planks, patient and hungry.",
  'abyss/dream_fragment': "A fragment of a dream hangs in the dark, a small bright room that seems to belong to someone else's memory. A table, a lamp and a window look out on an unchanging evening. The Watcher sits here, a drifting figure of light, and a small camp of warm quiet offers safe rest.",
  'abyss/eye_of_silence': "A vast chamber where sound ceases to exist, swallowed by the dark. A giant eye of dark glass floats in the center, unblinking and watching. You can hear your own heartbeat and nothing else, and the pressure grows by the second. Shapes drift just beyond sight.",
  'abyss/hollow_throne': "A throne carved from the dark itself sits at the end of a long hall of black pillars, empty and cold. The air around it presses against you, and a faint voice whispers of kingship and ruin. Dust drifts in slow spirals, and the shadows on the walls move in the wrong direction.",
  'abyss/edge_of_nothing': "The last ledge of reality, a narrow shelf of stone with nothing beyond it. The sky is empty, the void is silent, and the pull of oblivion is almost gentle. A single gust of cold wind brings the smell of rain from some other world. It is the loneliest place in existence.",
});

Object.assign(D, {
  'town/implant_lab': "A sterile white lab tucked behind the Chrome Clinic, humming with cold air filters and the soft tick of sterilizing lamps. Rows of sealed trays hold neural implants, each priced like a small house and each tagged with a Mark number. A surgeon in a clean suit logs your credit chip without a word. Type `list` to see the series. Install Mk I first and upgrade in order; the old implant is traded in for half its price. Each costs a little Aura.",
  'town/hall_of_rebirth': "A round chamber of white stone and humming cables, lit from below by a pool of slow, glowing water. Names of those who came before are etched into the wall, each followed by a number. The air smells of rain and ozone, and the water ripples when you step near it. At level 40, you may step into the pool and be reborn as something new. Type `remort` for the details and your choices.",
});

Object.assign(D, {
  'town/salvage_exchange': "A cramped trading post stacked with crates, hanging scales and sorting bins labeled in three languages. The salvager behind the counter weighs whatever you can dig, pick or catch, and pays 60% of its value, better than any other shop in the sprawl. The basics are on sale for crafters, too. Type `list` to see the stock, `sell materials` to sell your gathered goods at once. The room smells of river water, rust and dried herbs.",
});

module.exports = D;
